.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.env

# ---- policy: ops-policy.pdf p1 §10 ------------------------------------------------------
# "Customer and operational data ... must not be published, uploaded to public
# repositories or shared beyond the engagement team."
#
# The assignment brief asks for a public repository containing the data files. That
# conflicts with the client's own rulebook and the two cannot both be satisfied. On the
# user's instruction the policy wins: the data stays out of the repository. The service
# reads it from data/input/ at run time, so nothing about running the project changes.
#
# Revisit only if the client confirms in writing that publishing is permitted.
data/input/*
!data/input/.gitkeep
!data/input/README.md

# The trained model IS committed: the brief requires a repository that runs, and the
# model is a build output of this repo, not customer data. It is 419 KB and contains
# learned coefficients only — no request text, no identifiers.
#
# predictions.csv is committed too: it IS the deliverable. It holds request_id and team
# only, no customer text, so §10 does not reach it.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/.gitkeep
!artifacts/model.joblib
!artifacts/metrics.json
!artifacts/predictions.csv

# Audit outputs. These quote request text back, so they follow the same rule as the data.
artifacts/audit.txt
artifacts/errors_holdout.csv
artifacts/errors_holdout_labelled.csv
artifacts/confusion_holdout.csv
artifacts/policy.txt
artifacts/predictions_with_confidence.csv
artifacts/form_values.json
artifacts/state.json